          "layout": "text",
          "text": "RU-21-02-0173-310822/FACTSHEET \n \n \n \n \n \n \n‘One Nation One Ration Card’ \n \nMaking food security portable throughout the country \n \n100% Digitisation of Ration Cards \n \n(Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution) \n \nAugust 31, 2022 \n \n“With the help of One Nation-One Ration Card, we have ensured free ration to more than \n80 crore countrymen. This is the wonder of technology.” \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nPrime Minister, Narendra Modi \nOne Nation One Ration Card (ONORC) is a technology-driven scheme which is being \nimplemented by the Central Government for the nationwide portability of ration cards under \nthe National Food Security Act (NFSA).1 To address the difficulties of migrants, this system \nfor intra-State and inter-State portability of ration cards was launched by the Government of \nIndia on August 09, 2019.2 \n \nONORC is a countrywide innovation that allows all NFSA beneficiaries, particularly migrant \nbeneficiaries, to claim either full or part foodgrains from any Fair Price Shop (FPS) of their \nchoice in the country through the existing ration card with biometric/Aadhaar authentication in \n \n1 Factsheet Details: (pib.gov.in) \n2 https://transformingindia.mygov.in/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/ONORC-eng.pdf",
